IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`

-- Magna Carta (1215), English translation in McKechnie 1905: CHAPTERS 41 AND 42.
-- Merchants (41) and leaving and returning to the kingdom (42).
-- Terms the text does not define, taken as plain facts: merchant, the land at war with the King,
-- evil tolls, the ancient and right customs, time of war, short period, public policy,
-- imprisoned or outlawed in accordance with the law of the kingdom, allegiance
-- (see NOTES.md, "Terms the text does not define").
-- The text uses the passive throughout ("shall have", "shall be detained", "shall be safe") and
-- names no one who must provide the safe conduct, so these are decision functions and not
-- regulative rules (fork F41a).
-- GENERATED from tools/templates/mc15-ch41-42.l4.in by tools/build.py; edit the template.

§ `Chapters 41 and 42 -- merchants and travellers`

§§ `Chapter 41 -- merchants`

-- src:89 | All merchants shall have safe and secure exit from England, and entry to England, with the right to tarry there and to move about as well by land as by water, for buying and selling by the ancient and right customs, quit from all evil tolls,
-- src:89 | except (in time of war) such merchants as are of the land at war with us.
@ref Chapter 41 clause 41.1-41.2 (src:89)
GIVEN `the person is a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merchant is of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 41 -- the merchant has safe and secure exit, entry, stay and movement by land and by water` IS
    IF `the person is a merchant`
    THEN IF   `it is a time of war`
          AND `the merchant is of the land at war with the King`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except (in time of war) such merchants as are of the land at war with us".
         THEN `Not entitled`
         ELSE Entitled
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: except because "except" removes enemy merchants in time of war; the branch is reached by a person who is not a merchant).
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`

-- src:89 | All merchants shall have safe and secure exit from England, and entry to England, with the right to tarry there and to move about as well by land as by water, for buying and selling by the ancient and right customs, quit from all evil tolls,
-- src:89 | except (in time of war) such merchants as are of the land at war with us.
@ref Chapter 41 clause 41.1-41.2 (src:89)
GIVEN `the person is a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merchant is of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buying and selling is by the ancient and right customs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 41 -- the merchant may buy and sell` IS
    IF `the person is a merchant`
    THEN IF   `it is a time of war`
          AND `the merchant is of the land at war with the King`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except (in time of war) such merchants as are of the land at war with us".
         THEN `Not entitled`
         ELSE IF `the buying and selling is by the ancient and right customs`
              THEN Entitled
              -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: except because "except" removes enemy merchants in time of war; the case turns on "for buying and selling by the ancient and right customs", which is not a named word (F64c)).
              ELSE `Entitlement not covered`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: except because "except" removes enemy merchants in time of war; the branch is reached by a person who is not a merchant).
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`

-- "quit from all evil tolls": a toll that is not evil is not spoken to.  The merchants the
-- exception removes are not quit of tolls either.
-- src:89 | All merchants shall have safe and secure exit from England, and entry to England, with the right to tarry there and to move about as well by land as by water, for buying and selling by the ancient and right customs, quit from all evil tolls,
-- src:89 | except (in time of war) such merchants as are of the land at war with us.
@ref Chapter 41 clause 41.1-41.2 (src:89)
GIVEN `the person is a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merchant is of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the toll is an evil toll` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 41 -- a toll may be taken from the merchant` IS
    IF `the person is a merchant`
    THEN IF   `it is a time of war`
          AND `the merchant is of the land at war with the King`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except (in time of war) such merchants as are of the land at war with us".
         THEN `Not barred`
         ELSE IF `the toll is an evil toll`
              THEN Barred
              -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: except because "except" removes enemy merchants in time of war; the branch is reached by a toll that is not evil, where "evil" is undefined and the text speaks only to evil tolls).
              ELSE `Bar not covered`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: except because "except" removes enemy merchants in time of war; the branch is reached by a person who is not a merchant).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- 41.3: "such" merchants, those excepted in 41.2, "found in our land at the beginning of the war".
-- The text names no one who must detain them (fork F41a).
-- src:89 | And if such are found in our land at the beginning of the war, they shall be detained, without injury to their bodies or goods, until information be received by us, or by our chief justiciar, how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated;
@ref Chapter 41 clause 41.3 (src:89)
GIVEN `the person is a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merchant is of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merchant was found in the land at the beginning of the war` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information has been received by the King or his chief justiciar of how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is to be detained` IS
    IF   `the person is a merchant`
     AND `it is a time of war`
     AND `the merchant is of the land at war with the King`
    THEN IF `the merchant was found in the land at the beginning of the war`
         THEN IF `information has been received by the King or his chief justiciar of how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until information be received by us, or by our chief justiciar".
              THEN `Not obliged`
              ELSE Obliged
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "And if such are found in our land at the beginning of the war".
         ELSE `Not obliged`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if, until because "such" are the merchants excepted in 41.2, and the branch is reached by a person who is not one of them).
    ELSE `Obligation not covered`

-- src:89 | And if such are found in our land at the beginning of the war, they shall be detained, without injury to their bodies or goods, until information be received by us, or by our chief justiciar, how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated;
@ref Chapter 41 clause 41.3 (src:89)
GIVEN `the person is a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merchant is of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merchant was found in the land at the beginning of the war` IS A BOOLEAN
